Subject: [PATCH] hw/misc/bcm2835_property: Answer the reboot notification

Linux's raspberrypi-firmware driver sends NOTIFY_REBOOT before it
resets or powers off the machine, for the firmware to stop what it
drives. The model does not know the tag, so every reboot or power-off
of a Raspberry Pi 3 or 4 guest logs it as unimplemented.

Answer it with an empty value: the model has nothing to stop.
---
 hw/misc/bcm2835_property.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hw/misc/bcm2835_property.c b/hw/misc/bcm2835_property.c
index d4d9a03..48404a8 100644
--- a/hw/misc/bcm2835_property.c
+++ b/hw/misc/bcm2835_property.c
@@ -410,6 +410,14 @@ static void bcm2835_property_mbox_push(BCM2835PropertyState *s, uint32_t value)
             resplen = bcm2835_property_answer32(s, value, bufsize, 0);
             break;
 
+        case RPI_FWREQ_NOTIFY_REBOOT:
+            /*
+             * Sent before a reset or a power-off, for the firmware to stop
+             * what it drives; the model has nothing to stop
+             */
+            resplen = 0;
+            break;
+
         case RPI_FWREQ_VCHIQ_INIT:
             bcm2835_property_put32(s, value, bufsize, 0, 0);
             resplen = VCHI_BUSADDR_SIZE;
